.TH DNS_DFD 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
dns_domain_fromdot \- Convert a DNS domain name from dot-separated format to wire format

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/dns.h>

.IB int
.IB dns_domain_fromdot
.IB (char** out, const char* buf, size_t n);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBdns_domain_fromdot\fR function converts a DNS domain name from dot-separated format to wire format. The function takes three arguments:

.TP
.IB out
A pointer to a pointer that will be set to the converted domain name.
.TP
.IB buf
A pointer to the input buffer containing the dot-separated domain name.
.TP
.IB n
The length of the input buffer.

The function returns 1 on success and 0 on failure. If the function fails, it sets \fIerrno\fR to an appropriate error code.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBdns_domain_fromdot\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/dns.h>

int main() {
    char* out = NULL;
    const char* buf = "example.com";
    size_t n = strlen(buf);

    if (dns_domain_fromdot(&out, buf, n) != 1) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Error: %s\n", strerror(errno));
        return 1;
    }

    printf("Converted domain name: %s\n", out);

    free(out);

    return 0;
}
.nef